[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=Samsung QM Series RS-232 control, including the QM75C.\\Models named||1
  Cmn2=by the older wrapper: QM32C, QM43C, QM50C, QM55C, QM65C, QM75C,||1
  Cmn3=QM85C, QM98C.\\Protocol: Samsung Multiple Display Control (MDC).
  Cmn4=||1Not tried on a live display.\\\\Connection\\9600 baud, 8 data bits,||1
  Cmn5=no parity, 1 stop bit, no flow control.\\Display pin 2 is Tx, pin||1
  Cmn6=3 is Rx, pin 5 is ground.\\A Crestron COM port receives on pin 2||1
  Cmn7=and transmits on pin 3, so use a straight-through cable.\\\\Display||1
  Cmn8=ID\\Display_Id must match the ID in the display menu. The factory||1
  Cmn9=ID is often not 1.\\Set the display to the same number, or set Display_Id||1
  Cmn10=to 255 to address every display on the chain.\\\\Packet\\AA command||1
  Cmn11=ID length data checksum\\Every byte is hexadecimal. The checksum||1
  Cmn12=is the low byte of the sum of every byte except the AA header.\\
  Cmn13=A set has length 1 and one data byte. A query has length 0 and no||1
  Cmn14=data byte.\\Power on, ID 1: AA 11 01 01 01 14\\Power query, ID 1:
  Cmn15=||1AA 11 01 00 12\\\\Reply\\AA FF ID length A-or-N command value checksum\\
  Cmn16=A (hex 41) is success. N (hex 4E) is failure. Nak_FB pulses on failure.
  Cmn17=\\Last_Status shows the result in words.\\\\Commands on this symbol\\
  Cmn18=Power          11    00 off, 01 on\\Volume         12    00 through||1
  Cmn19=100\\Mute           13    00 off, 01 on\\Input          14    21||1
  Cmn20=HDMI 1, 23 HDMI 2, 31 HDMI 3, 25 DisplayPort, 20 MagicInfo\\Picture||1
  Cmn21=size   15    00 auto, 01 16:9, 04 zoom, 0C wide fit\\Volume step||1
  Cmn22=||362    00 up, 01 down\\\\Any other MDC command can be sent with||1
  Cmn23=Raw_Command, Raw_Data, Send_Raw_Set, and Send_Raw_Get.\\Send_Raw_Set||1
  Cmn24=sends one data byte. Send_Raw_Get sends a query.\\\\Poll_Enable||1
  Cmn25=asks for power, volume, mute, input, and picture size, one query||1
  Cmn26=each Poll_Interval.
[END]
